[38;2;124;124;124mpower of t with a nonzero coefficient is t⁵ (if a ≠ 0), t³ (if a = 0, b ≠ 0), or[0m[38;2;124;124;124mt¹ (if a = b = 0, c ≠ 0). In all cases, the degree of p(t) is odd (5, 3, or 1 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrespectively).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince p(t) is a polynomial of odd degree with real coefficients, it has at least[0m[38;2;124;124;124mone real root. Since its degree is at most 5, it has at most 5 real roots [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(counting multiplicity; the number of distinct real roots is at most 5).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore, M ∩ λ is nonempty (at least one real root) and finite (at most 5 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpoints).[0m

